  "caveats": [
    "1. Unbroken S_3-equivariance on Bring's 3-generation space projGen3 forces b = c in S(a,b,c), leaving a degenerate 2D doublet (lambda_1 = lambda_2 = a - b); splitting all three charged leptons strictly requires chiral symmetry breaking S_3 -> Z_3 (b != c). 2. While Temperley-Lieb Convention-D Wedderburn trace weights (y_3, 2 y_21) achieve EXACT singlet-doublet equipartition (1/2 = 1/2, Q = 2/3) at the classical point q = 1, at finite q_0 = 1.10997858... they shift strictly below 2/3 by -(q_0 - q_0^-1)^2 / (3(q_0^2 + q_0^-2)) = -0.00712859 (-1.0693% relative, >10700 sigma from empirical Q_exp = 0.66666050(66)). 3. Because the empirical Brannen-Koide phase theta_exp = 0.22222205... rad lies within 0.03958 rad of the electron chiral zero pi/12 = 0.26179939..., logarithmic mass-ratio sensitivities are >50x (d ln(m_mu/m_e)/d theta = 56.14, d ln(m_tau/m_e)/d theta = 51.23), so none of the six un-tuned q_0 phase expressions simultaneously matches m_mu/m_e and m_tau/m_e within 1% (best q_0 phase 2(q_0-1) misses by -11.66% and -10.67%, whereas the q-independent rational benchmark theta = 2/9 = 2/[3]_{q=1}^2 matches to +9.83 ppm on m_mu/m_e and +70.41 ppm on m_tau/m_e, and feeding QOU's zero-CAL-2 Vol(4_1)/hbar_{q_0}^2 into exact Q = 2/3 predicts m_tau/m_e = 3477.4423, +61.63 ppm). Any finite-q_0 Koide closure remains gated behind Rule-13a zero-instance class KoideCirculantEquipartitionHypothesis."
